# MONARK Dojo same-origin proxy snippet (the reread of the head of the day by /dojo). Deployed by an act under go, never by CI.
#
# INSERT the `handle_path /dojo-served/*` block below INSIDE the EXISTING vitrine site block (`monarkgate.tech, www.monarkgate.tech
# { ... }`), BEFORE its `reverse_proxy localhost:3000`: a path matcher wins over the catch-all proxy. The prefix sits OUTSIDE the page
# route: /dojo and /dojo/* stay with Next (a `/dojo-served/*` matcher matches neither). It relays GET of three closed paths of the
# Dojo host and nothing else: timeline.jsonl, lines/<sha256>.jsonl, dojo/pubkey.json; any other method or path answers 404. The Host
# header is set to the upstream (HTTPS upstream: Caddy does it by itself since v2.11.0; set here because the installed version is
# read at the deploy act). Cache-Control of every relayed answer is replaced by no-store, so no edge in front of the site keeps a
# served timeline (the edge's cache status is measured at the deploy act). TLS to the upstream is checked: no tls_insecure_* option.
# Back up, validate, reload, then curl the three paths; rollback = delete these lines and reload (motif of the Narabi snippet).

    handle_path /dojo-served/* {
        @read {
            method GET
            path /timeline.jsonl /lines/* /dojo/pubkey.json
        }
        handle @read {
            reverse_proxy https://dojo.monarkgate.tech {
                header_up Host {upstream_hostport}
                header_down Cache-Control "no-store"
            }
        }
        handle {
            respond 404
        }
    }
